{# The page shows the stored (medium) file and previous/next browse it, the high resolution being fetched only when it is asked for - the gesture is UiBundle's c975LUi:Image:Zoom, written here first and moved there so a planche or any other picture could open the same way, this bundle now naming the two files and the words the link is announced with #}

{# The photo is what the page is for, so it is named in both places it appears - a media whose title is empty falls back on its category's, which the entity holds as NOT NULL #}
{% set mediaAlt = media.title|default(media.category.title|default('')) %}
<twig:c975LUi:Image:Zoom
    src="{{ media.filename }}"
    highres="{{ media.highresFilename }}"
    alt="{{ mediaAlt }}"
    label="{{ 'label.gallery_see_high_resolution'|trans({}, 'gallery') }}"
    class="media gallery-media-display"
/>
